 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Out on the street, Max gives his granddad's old watch to an old man. Here it is in Russian.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На, держись, старик.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Это мне?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Тебе. Тебе нужнее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Спасибо, сынок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Не за что.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Дай бог тебе здоровья.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now the words up close.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На, держись, старик.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here. Hang in there, old man.' Russian hands things over with na, a little word like 'here, take it', and derzhis literally means 'hold on'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Это мне?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Is this for me?' Russian needs no verb here: eto mne, literally 'this to me'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Тебе. Тебе нужнее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'For you. You need it more.' The word nuzhnee means 'more needed', so tebe nuzhnee is literally 'to you it's more needed'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Спасибо, сынок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thank you, son.' Older people in Russian call a young man synok, literally 'little son', even a stranger.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Не за что.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Don't mention it.' The reply ne za chto literally means 'not for anything', the usual answer to spasibo.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Дай бог тебе здоровья.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'God bless you.' Russian says dai bog tebe zdorovya, literally 'may God give you health', a thank-you you hear from older people. Here's the street scene again.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На, держись, старик.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Это мне?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Тебе. Тебе нужнее.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Спасибо, сынок.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Не за что.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Дай бог тебе здоровья.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max walks on, and the old man keeps the watch. In Russian, the polite reply to spasibo is ne za chto, literally 'not for anything'. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "old_man",
   "t": "Счастливо!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
